<section style="padding:80px 24px 8px;background:#fff;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <div class="rich"><p>If a roofer just told you the panels have to come off before they can touch your roof, here's the short answer. In 2026, <a href="/solar-detach-reset-greeley/">solar detach and reset</a> in the Greeley area runs <strong>$200 to $500 per panel</strong>, which puts a typical 20-panel home array at <strong>around $3,500</strong> for the full job. That covers removal, safe storage while the roof gets replaced, reinstallation, and electrical recommissioning so the system comes back on the way it should.</p><p>The good news for hail claims: on a covered roof claim, the detach and reset line item is typically paid by the insurance claim, not out of your pocket. Below you'll find a full price table, the factors that push jobs up or down, and answers to the questions homeowners ask us mid-reroof. Every job gets a free written estimate, so you'll have a firm number before anything comes off the roof.</p></div>
  </div></section>
